---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;

const toc = [
  { label: 'Getting an Account',  id: 'enrollment' },
  { label: 'The Cluster',         id: 'cluster' },
  { label: 'First Login',         id: 'access' },
  { label: 'Files & Storage',     id: 'storage' },
  { label: 'House Rules',         id: 'rules' },
  { label: 'Getting Help',        id: 'help' },
];
---

<DocsLayout title="Welcome & Onboarding" toc={toc}>

  <h1>Welcome & Onboarding</h1>

  <p>
    Welcome to the <strong>Artificial Intelligence and Robotics Lab (AIRLab)</strong> at
    Politecnico di Milano. This guide covers <strong>polimi-cluster</strong>, the AIRLab
    high-performance computing (HPC) cluster: how to get an account, store your data, and run jobs.
  </p>

  <!-- ── Enrollment ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <h2 id="enrollment">Getting an Account</h2>

  <p>
    <strong>Every thesis student must enroll</strong>, even if you do not plan to use the cluster:
    enrollment also registers you as an AIRLab thesis student.
  </p>

  <ol class="steps">
    <li><span><strong>Lab access.</strong> Register as an AIRLab user at
      <a href="https://airlab.deib.polimi.it/life-in-airlab/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Life@AIRLab</a>
      to get access to Building 7.</span></li>
    <li><span><strong>Join Discord.</strong> Ask your co-advisor for an invite to the AIRLab Discord server.</span></li>
    <li><span><strong>Fill in the
      <a href="https://forms.cloud.microsoft/e/TLARAzW0nK" target="_blank" rel="noopener">enrollment form</a>.</strong></span></li>
    <li><span><strong>Ask a co-advisor to enroll you.</strong> In your thesis channel on Discord, they run
      <code>/hpc enroll @you</code>. PhD students and external users: any Discord channel you are in works.</span></li>
    <li><span><strong>Check your email.</strong> You will receive your username, a temporary password,
      and connection instructions. Your VPN access request is started automatically during enrollment.</span></li>
    <li><span><strong>Set up the VPN.</strong> Once access is granted, install
      <a href="https://www.ict.polimi.it/network/vpn/?lang=en" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GlobalProtect</a>.
      You need it to reach the cluster from outside the AIRLab network.</span></li>
  </ol>

  <!-- ── The Cluster ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <h2 id="cluster">The Cluster</h2>

  <p>
    You log in to a single machine, the <strong>login node</strong> (<code>matteucci-vm-1</code>),
    and ask <strong>Slurm</strong> for CPUs, memory, and GPUs. Slurm runs your job on a compute node
    with free resources. You never pick or SSH into a compute node yourself.
  </p>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Compute node</th><th>CPUs</th><th>GPUs</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><strong>caladan</strong></td><td>192</td><td>8 × NVIDIA L4 (24 GB)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>magrathea</strong></td><td>112</td><td>8 × NVIDIA Quadro RTX 6000 (24 GB)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>akira</strong></td><td>256</td><td>6 × NVIDIA RTX A6000 (48 GB)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>arrakis</strong></td><td>192</td><td>6 × NVIDIA RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell Max-Q (96 GB)</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="callout callout-danger">
    <svg class="w-5 h-5 flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5 text-red-500" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
         stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
      <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/>
      <line x1="15" y1="9" x2="9" y2="15"/><line x1="9" y1="9" x2="15" y2="15"/>
    </svg>
    <div class="text-sm leading-relaxed">
      <strong>The login node is for editing, file transfers, and submitting jobs only.</strong>
      Training, preprocessing, notebooks, and package installation go through Slurm
      (<a href={`${base}docs/slurm`}>Running Jobs</a>).
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ── First Login ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <h2 id="access">First Login</h2>

  <p>
    Use the IP address: over the VPN, internal DNS may not resolve the hostname. Then change your
    temporary password.
  </p>

  <CodeBlock
    lang="bash"
    filename="local machine"
    code={`ssh USERNAME@10.75.4.86
# or, when the hostname resolves: ssh USERNAME@matteucci-vm-1.inside.dei.polimi.it

passwd    # on the cluster: current password, then the new one twice`}
  />

  <p>
    Never share your password or account. Next, set up an SSH key and a short alias:
    see <a href={`${base}docs/shell#ssh-keys`}>Shell &amp; Remote Access</a>.
  </p>

  <!-- ── Files & Storage ───────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <h2 id="storage">Files & Storage</h2>

  <p>
    Your home is on <strong>megaverse</strong>, the lab's persistent network storage, mounted on the
    login node and on every compute node: what you save on the login node is visible to your jobs.
  </p>

  <CodeBlock
    lang="text"
    filename="your home directory"
    code={`~  =  /megaverse/storage/USERNAME      ← code, environments, results
└── dataset/
    ├── shared/                        ← datasets shared across the lab
    └── private/                       ← your own datasets`}
  />

  <ul>
    <li>Check your usage with <code>du -sh ~</code> and free space with <code>df -h ~</code>.</li>
    <li>Avoid millions of tiny files: prefer archives or dataset formats (<code>tar</code>, HDF5, LMDB, WebDataset shards).</li>
    <li>Keep important data in your home or dataset directories, not in node-local temporary folders.</li>
  </ul>

  <!-- ── House Rules ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <h2 id="rules">House Rules</h2>

  <table>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>📏 <strong>Request only what you use</strong></td><td>Idle CPUs and GPUs still block others and count against your <a href={`${base}docs/slurm#queues`}>fair-share</a>.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>♻️ <strong>Reproducible environments</strong></td><td>Conda plus an exported <code>environment.yml</code> (<a href={`${base}docs/environments`}>how</a>).</td></tr>
      <tr><td>🔀 <strong>Code on Git</strong></td><td>A private GitHub repository, with your co-advisors as members.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>📝 <strong>Documented</strong></td><td>A <code>README.md</code> that lets a stranger reproduce your results.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <!-- ── Getting Help ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <h2 id="help">Getting Help</h2>

  <p>
    Ask in the <strong>👨🏻‍🏭servers-administration</strong> channel on Discord. Include your username,
    the job ID, the script or command you ran, the relevant log lines, and what you expected to happen.
  </p>

  <div class="callout callout-danger">
    <svg class="w-5 h-5 flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5 text-red-500" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
         stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
      <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/>
      <line x1="15" y1="9" x2="9" y2="15"/><line x1="9" y1="9" x2="15" y2="15"/>
    </svg>
    <div class="text-sm leading-relaxed">
      Never post passwords, private SSH keys, tokens, or confidential data on Discord.
    </div>
  </div>

</DocsLayout>
